Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.7.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.7.0 fixes the BLACK content area left over from 0.6.0. 0.6.0 built its own presentation manager with [[UIScenePresentationManager alloc] _initWithScene:scene]; the whole chain ran, the presentation view came back real, and nothing crashed - but the panel stayed black, because a self-made manager is not registered in the scene's own presenter-owner machinery, so the presenter never reaches the "hosting" state and _UIScenePresentationView simply paints its backgroundColorWhileNotHosting (black). The one implementation that is publicly known to work on iOS 17 (khanhduytran0/FrontBoardAppLauncher, the same source LiveContainer's multitasking uses) always takes the presenter from the scene itself: presenter = [scene.uiPresentationManager createPresenterWithIdentifier:sceneID]; [presenter modifyPresentationContext:^(ctx){ ctx.appearanceStyle = 2; }]; [presenter activate]; [view addSubview:presenter.presentationView]. It also creates the scene with foreground=YES / level=1 / frame / displayConfiguration, i.e. it tells FrontBoard the scene is live and on screen. 0.7.0 does the same with four routes: hostRoute=3 (default) adopts the target app's EXISTING scene, uses THAT scene's own uiPresentationManager, and first runs a P0 step that pushes foreground=YES / level=1 / portrait into the scene settings; hostRoute=4 mirrors FrontBoardAppLauncher exactly and builds its own scene via [[FBSceneManager sharedInstance] createSceneWithDefinition:initialParameters:] before presenting it; hostRoute=2 is the old 0.6.0 path kept for A/B comparison; hostRoute=1 is the old SpringBoard host view controller. forceActivate has been REMOVED - on device it killed SpringBoard inside the 20 s survival window (crash attribution: crashedStep=S7-settle) and its effect is now achieved non-invasively by updating scene settings. The config file is now re-read on every host attempt, so parameters can be A/B tested by simply tapping an app row again instead of respringing (respringing kills the target app's scene). Every step is instrumented into /var/mobile/MF-host-step.txt (S1..S7 plus P0..P6), and /var/mobile/MF-presenter-report.txt now also records scene.settings, presenter isActive/isHosting and the layer counts, which is exactly what distinguishes "presenter not hosting" from "scene has no layers" from "layers present but geometry wrong". DISABLED BY DEFAULT: needs /var/mobile/MultiFloat.plist with enabled=true AND hostEnabled=true. Crash-guard marker still makes a crash loop impossible. No hooks are installed. Log: /var/mobile/MultiFloat.log
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
